{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00592",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 0.89,
      "end_seconds": 10.93,
      "duration_seconds": 10.04,
      "text": "Morning, Joan, morning, Helen. Dreadful weather. Did you manage to park alright, or is the car park a disaster again?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 13.4,
      "end_seconds": 29.79,
      "duration_seconds": 16.39,
      "text": "Mum insisted on being right by the door, so I circled for twenty minutes. Anyway, we're here for the check-up after she was so poorly last month."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 31.0,
      "end_seconds": 37.75,
      "duration_seconds": 6.75,
      "text": "I like to be close to the door, dear. It's the rain."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 40.32,
      "end_seconds": 47.18,
      "duration_seconds": 6.86,
      "text": "Quite sensible. So, Joan, how have you been in yourself since then?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 49.59,
      "end_seconds": 54.52,
      "duration_seconds": 4.93,
      "text": "Oh, much better, thank you. Just ticking along, really."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 56.17,
      "end_seconds": 62.3,
      "duration_seconds": 6.13,
      "text": "Good. Let's talk about your chest. Have you been coughing at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 63.22,
      "end_seconds": 67.61,
      "duration_seconds": 4.39,
      "text": "No, I'm not coughing. Not that I've noticed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 70.45,
      "end_seconds": 77.65,
      "duration_seconds": 7.2,
      "text": "Mum, you are. You're coughing at night. I can hear you through the wall."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 79.88,
      "end_seconds": 86.13,
      "duration_seconds": 6.25,
      "text": "Am I? I don't notice it, dear. I sleep like a log."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 88.75,
      "end_seconds": 97.09,
      "duration_seconds": 8.34,
      "text": "Okay, I'll keep both views in mind. Helen, how often do you hear it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 98.62,
      "end_seconds": 106.53,
      "duration_seconds": 7.91,
      "text": "Most nights, a dry little cough. It doesn't go on for long, but it's there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 108.92,
      "end_seconds": 115.72,
      "duration_seconds": 6.8,
      "text": "Thank you. Joan, what about the stairs, do you get puffed out?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 118.38,
      "end_seconds": 127.79,
      "duration_seconds": 9.41,
      "text": "No, I don't get puffed out. I do the stairs two at a time. Well, one at a time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 130.46,
      "end_seconds": 135.8,
      "duration_seconds": 5.34,
      "text": "Lovely. Now, which pills are you taking at the moment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 138.43,
      "end_seconds": 145.07,
      "duration_seconds": 6.64,
      "text": "Just the blood pressure one, and a stomach one. Helen has the list."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 147.82,
      "end_seconds": 154.96,
      "duration_seconds": 7.14,
      "text": "Amlodipine, 5 mg, once a day. And omeprazole, 20 mg, in the mornings."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 157.17,
      "end_seconds": 163.76,
      "duration_seconds": 6.59,
      "text": "Thanks. And the amlodipine is for your high blood pressure, is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 165.07,
      "end_seconds": 170.65,
      "duration_seconds": 5.58,
      "text": "Yes, that's what I've got. High blood pressure, for years now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 172.63,
      "end_seconds": 177.76,
      "duration_seconds": 5.13,
      "text": "Have you had any operations, Joan, at any time?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 179.16,
      "end_seconds": 186.53,
      "duration_seconds": 7.37,
      "text": "A hip replacement, about five years ago. Best thing I ever did."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 187.96,
      "end_seconds": 191.52,
      "duration_seconds": 3.56,
      "text": "Excellent. And have you ever smoked?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 193.88,
      "end_seconds": 202.53,
      "duration_seconds": 8.65,
      "text": "I gave up smoking twenty years ago. Forty a day... no, twenty a day. Ha."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 204.04,
      "end_seconds": 212.52,
      "duration_seconds": 8.48,
      "text": "Good for you. Let me check your numbers now. Pop your sleeve up for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 230.23,
      "end_seconds": 240.49,
      "duration_seconds": 10.26,
      "text": "Blood pressure 134 over 76, pulse 82, temperature 36.7 degrees Celsius, breathing 16 breaths per minute, and oxygen 96 percent."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 242.23,
      "end_seconds": 244.5,
      "duration_seconds": 2.27,
      "text": "Is that good?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 253.85,
      "end_seconds": 264.86,
      "duration_seconds": 11.01,
      "text": "Those are all pleasing. Now I'll listen to your chest, so take some nice deep breaths in and out."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 286.72,
      "end_seconds": 292.49,
      "duration_seconds": 5.77,
      "text": "Your chest sounds clear on both sides. You can relax now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 293.3,
      "end_seconds": 296.2,
      "duration_seconds": 2.9,
      "text": "That's a relief to hear."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 298.05,
      "end_seconds": 313.14,
      "duration_seconds": 15.09,
      "text": "Let me explain my thinking. After being as poorly as you were, we like to look at the lungs again, to make sure everything has cleared."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 314.97,
      "end_seconds": 322.81,
      "duration_seconds": 7.84,
      "text": "Your numbers and the way your chest sounds suggest the lungs are healing as expected."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 325.2,
      "end_seconds": 328.54,
      "duration_seconds": 3.34,
      "text": "So do I need anything more?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 329.88,
      "end_seconds": 339.83,
      "duration_seconds": 9.95,
      "text": "I'd like to arrange a chest X-ray, just to be certain. It's the only way to see the lungs properly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 341.36,
      "end_seconds": 345.23,
      "duration_seconds": 3.87,
      "text": "Does she have to book it herself?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 348.07,
      "end_seconds": 355.69,
      "duration_seconds": 7.62,
      "text": "No, my team will send the request today, and radiology will ring you with a time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 357.11,
      "end_seconds": 366.77,
      "duration_seconds": 9.66,
      "text": "If the X-ray still shows a shadow, I'll see you again and we'll decide together what comes next."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 368.55,
      "end_seconds": 372.03,
      "duration_seconds": 3.48,
      "text": "And what if it's all clear?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 372.84,
      "end_seconds": 380.4,
      "duration_seconds": 7.56,
      "text": "Then you carry on as you are, and there's no need to come back about this."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 382.91,
      "end_seconds": 388.76,
      "duration_seconds": 5.85,
      "text": "And Mum's cough at night? Should we do something about that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 389.82,
      "end_seconds": 399.66,
      "duration_seconds": 9.84,
      "text": "Let's see what the X-ray shows first. Helen, jot down which nights you hear it, so we have something concrete."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 401.87,
      "end_seconds": 404.43,
      "duration_seconds": 2.56,
      "text": "I will. Thanks, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 405.58,
      "end_seconds": 410.18,
      "duration_seconds": 4.6,
      "text": "Thank you, dear. Is it still raining?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 411.89,
      "end_seconds": 420.18,
      "duration_seconds": 8.29,
      "text": "Hard as ever. Take an umbrella, and mind the kerb on the way out."
    }
  ]
}
